index 4479b53..6e9bae5 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,40 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Account settings and passkeys
+
+Signed-in readers can open **Account settings** from the header at
+`/devtools-times/account/settings`. Password sign-in is verified by the existing
+Times identity service; the app then creates an HttpOnly, same-site server session.
+Readers can register a passkey, rename its local label, remove it, or update their
+account display name. Registered passkeys can also be used on the sign-in page.
+
+The app requires Node.js 22.13 or newer for built-in SQLite. Accounts and verified
+credentials are persisted in `.data/accounts.sqlite`; sessions live in
+`.data/sessions`. Mount `.data` on persistent storage for a single-instance
+deployment. Set `ACCOUNT_DB_PATH` to relocate the database. For multiple instances,
+use shared credential and session stores rather than separate local files.
+
+Set `WEBAUTHN_RP_ID` to the public hostname (without a scheme or port), and
+`WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN` to the exact public origin when deploying behind a proxy. They
+default to the incoming request hostname and origin. WebAuthn requires HTTPS
+(localhost is allowed). Existing credentials belonging to another RP, origin, or
+identity service cannot be imported by the browser; connect that service's
+credential store if migrating an existing passkey installation.
+
+Credential changes are authorized against the session's account and RP. The
+complete server list is signaled to compatible password managers on page load,
+registration, and deletion. Account display-name changes use the user-details
+signal; a passkey nickname is only a server label. Signal failures do not undo
+saved changes, and readers can retry synchronization. Unsupported browsers get
+manual password-manager guidance.
+
+Provider metadata is a bundled subset of the
+[community AAGUID registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids),
+with a generic fallback for unknown or anonymized authenticators. It is display
+metadata, not a security assertion.
+
+Run `pnpm run build` for a production build and `node --test tests/*.test.mjs`
+on Node.js 22.18+ for isolated storage and synchronization tests. No running server
+is needed for these checks.
